course: dictionary
lesson: 15049
title: Retrain: learning again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To retrain means to learn new skills, usually so you can do a different job. «Mum decided to retrain as a nurse.» The word as tells you the new job, and retrain tells you she is learning something new to do it.
explain: You can also retrain an animal or a person by teaching them again. «The dog kept barking, so the trainer began to retrain it.» The dog already knows something, and now it is being taught a better way. Look at the words around retrain to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap check. Put in a simple meaning, such as learn new skills, and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «She signed up for a retraining course at the college.» A course to learn new skills fits the sentence well.
fact: To retrain means to learn new skills, usually for a different job.
fact: To retrain someone or an animal means to teach them again or teach them something new.
fact: «Retrain as» is used when someone learns a new job, as in «retrain as a teacher».
fact: A «retraining course» is a class that teaches new skills for work.
fact: Retrain is a verb. Its other forms are retrains, retrained and retraining.
exercise: «Mum decided to retrain as a nurse.» What does retrain mean here? | *Learn new skills for a different job | Buy a new house | Sing in a choir | Give up work for ever
exercise: «The dog had learned bad habits, so the trainer began to retrain it.» What does the trainer do? | Takes the dog for a long walk | Sells the dog | *Teaches the dog something new to replace the bad habits | Gives the dog a bath
exercise: «She signed up for a retraining course at the college.» Find and copy the word that shows the course is about learning new skills. | course | *retraining | college | signed
test: «After the factory closed, Dad had to retrain as a plumber.» What does retrain mean? | Lose his job for good | Work the same job again | *Learn new skills for a new job | Move to a new country
test: «Can you retrain a dog that barks too much?» What does retrain mean in this sentence? | *Teach the dog again so it stops barking | Let the dog run free | Give the dog a new name | Buy a bigger bed for the dog
exam: Which sentence uses retrain to mean teach again? | *The dog was retrained to walk nicely on a lead | The train was late this morning | We played football in the park | Dad went to the shop to buy bread
